          "en": "Supreme People's Court\nLetter on the Question of What Kind of Case a People's Court Should Accept\nWhere a Lawsuit Is Filed Against the Act of the Government or a Competent Department\nof Real Estate Administration Confirming Title to a Disputed House\n17 April 1993      Fa Han No. 33 [1993]\nTo the higher people's court of Sichuan Province:\nYour court's request for instructions, Chuan Gao Fa No. 27 [1993], on the question of what kind of case a people's court should accept where a lawsuit is filed against the act of the government or the competent department of real estate administration confirming title to a disputed house, has been received. After study, the reply is as follows:\nWhere a party, being dissatisfied with a decision of a people's government or a competent department of real estate administration confirming title in a dispute over house ownership, files a lawsuit, the people's court shall accept it as an administrative case."
