          "en": "Supreme People's Court\non the Limitation Period for the Right of Claim of a Carrier for Compensation\nagainst the Shipper, Consignee or Holder of a Bill of Lading\nin the Carriage of Goods by Sea: Reply\nFa Shi No. 3 [1997]\n(Adopted at the 921st meeting of the Judicial Committee of the Supreme People's Court on 11 July 1997; promulgated by announcement of the Supreme People's Court on 5 August 1997; coming into force on 7 August 1997)\nTo the higher people's court of Shandong Province:\nYour court's request for instructions, Lu Fa Jing No. 74 [1996], 'Request for Instructions on the Limitation Period for the Right to Claim Compensation', has been received. After study, the reply is as follows:\nPending provision by the relevant law, the right of claim of a carrier seeking compensation from a shipper, consignee or holder of a bill of lading in respect of the carriage of goods by sea shall be governed, by analogy, by paragraph 1 of Article 257 of the Maritime Code of the People's Republic of China; the limitation period shall be one year, counted from the date on which the right holder knew or ought to have known that his right had been infringed.\nThis is our reply."
