        "text": {
          "en": "The Supreme People's Court\nReply on the Characterisation of the Act of a Village Group Leader Who Illegally Takes\nPossession of Public Property by Taking Advantage of His Position\nFa Shi No. 12 [1999]\n(Adopted at the 1,069th meeting of the Judicial Committee of the Supreme People's Court on 18 June 1999; promulgated by announcement of the Supreme People's Court on 25 June 1999; coming into force on 3 July 1999)\nTo the Higher People's Court of Sichuan Province:\nThe request for instructions of your court, Chuan Gao Fa No. 224 [1998], entitled \"Request for Instructions on the Question How the Conduct of a Village Group Leader Who Embezzles Public Property by Taking Advantage of His Position Should Be Characterised\", has been received. After study, the reply is as follows:\nWhere a village group leader, by taking advantage of his position, illegally takes the collective property of the village group into his own possession, and the amount is relatively large, he shall, in accordance with paragraph 1 of Article 271 of the Criminal Law, be convicted and punished for the crime of embezzlement by taking advantage of duty.\nThis is our reply."
        },
