          "en": "The Supreme People's Court\nReply on Whether a People's Court Shall Accept an Application for Retrial\nby a Party Dissatisfied with an Order of a People's Court Setting Aside\nan Arbitral Award\nFa Shi No. 6 [1999]\n(Adopted at the 1,042nd meeting of the Judicial Committee of the Supreme People's Court on 29 January 1999; promulgated by announcement of the Supreme People's Court on 11 February 1999; coming into force on 16 February 1999)\nTo the Higher People's Court of Shaanxi Province:\nThe request for instructions of your court, Shan Gao Fa No. 78 [1998], entitled \"Request for Instructions on Whether a People's Court Shall Accept an Application for Retrial by a Party Dissatisfied with an Order of a People's Court Setting Aside an Arbitral Award\", has been received. After study, the reply is as follows:\nIn accordance with the spirit of Article 9 of the Arbitration Law of the People's Republic of China, where a party, being dissatisfied with a ruling of a people's court setting aside an arbitral award, applies for retrial, the people's court shall not accept the application.\nThis is our reply."
