          "en": "Supreme People's Court\nInterpretation on Issues Concerning the Application of Law in Handling Cases of\nAltering Postage Stamps or Reselling Altered Postage Stamps\nFa Shi No. 41 [2000]\n(Adopted at the 1,139th meeting of the Judicial Committee of the Supreme People's Court on 15 November 2000; promulgated by announcement of the Supreme People's Court on 5 December 2000; coming into force on 9 December 2000)\nIn order to correctly apply the Criminal Law, the issues concerning the application of law in the trial of cases of altering postage stamps or reselling altered postage stamps are interpreted as follows:\nWhere the amount involved in altering postage stamps or reselling altered postage stamps is relatively large, the person shall be convicted and punished in accordance with paragraph 1 of Article 227 of the Criminal Law."
