        "text": {
          "en": "Supreme People's Court\nReply on the Question of the Scope of Agency of Entrusted Agents\nin Civil Litigation in Execution Proceedings\n23 January 1997, Fa Fu No. 1 [1997]\nthe Higher People's Court of Shaanxi Province:\nThe request for instructions No. 78 [1996] of the Shaanxi Higher People's Court, 'On Whether the Scope of Agency of an Entrusted Agent in Litigation Includes Execution Proceedings', has been received. After study, the reply is as follows:\nUnder the provisions of the Civil Procedure Law, a party in civil litigation is entitled to entrust an agent. Where a party entrusts an agent, it shall submit to the people's court in accordance with law a power of attorney stating the matters entrusted and the specific scope of the agent's representation. If the party has not stated in the power of attorney whether the agent has the power of representation in execution proceedings and the specific matters of representation, the agent has no power of representation in execution proceedings and may not represent the party in directly collecting or disposing of the subject matter.\nThis is our reply."
        },
